(ii) The alien has passed the National Council Licensure Examination for registered nurses (NCLEX-RN);
(iii) The alien is a graduate of a nursing program in which the language of instruction was English;
(iv) The nursing program was located in Australia, Canada (except Quebec), Ireland, New Zealand, South Africa, the United Kingdom, or the United States; or in any other country designated by unanimous agreement of CGFNS and any equivalent credentialing organizations which have been approved for the certification of nurses and which are listed at paragraph (e) of this section; and
